fact WorkItem(id: "WI-974", description: some(value: "WI-956 item 4 fixed the gates it named and PROVED the class is live. The rest of typing.rs still asks `kind_of`, and this ticket carries the proof so the next reader does not re-derive it.\n\nTHE DATUM, measured over stdlib + anthill-stl (2598 distinct symbols):\n  - 68 symbols carry more than one category. 64 are [Entity, Sort] (the top-level `entity X(...)` sugar of §6.3), 4 are [Sort, Entity].\n  - So for 64 sorts, `kind_of(s) == Some(Sort)` is FALSE while `has_kind(s, Sort)` is TRUE.\n  - A name can also be [Entity, Sort, Operation] (`entity foo(k)` beside `operation foo(...)`), so the Operation direction diverges too.\n  - `kind_of`'s own doc (kb/mod.rs) already says it is for DISPLAY and that `has_kind` is the membership question.\n\nDRIVEN, not argued (wi956_kind_gate_tests, typing.rs):\n    entity Rec(n: Int64)\n    sort Rec\n      sort T = ?\n      operation peek(x: T) -> T\n    end\n  loads clean, and under `kind_of` `call_bracket_scopes(Rec.peek)` returned [] — the sort's own T missing from the bracket scopes. `has_kind` returns [\"T\"]. The same misread emptied the WI-565 bare-member hint.\n\nWHAT WI-956 FIXED (do not redo): the five `impl_parent_of_op` + kind gates, now one `impl_parent_sort_of_op`; `member_owning_sorts_for_bare`; `genuine_concrete_sort` (the shared filled_carrier_sort / ground_rigid_projection_if_concrete test); ground_rigid's Operation gate.\n\nWHAT IS LEFT — every remaining `kind_of(..) == Some(SymbolKind::..)` in typing.rs used as a TEST rather than for display. At the time of writing: ~4547, 6420, 7291, 8166, 9828, 10830, 14402(recheck), 18954, 18992, 22111, 26196, 26218, 27722, 28196, 29625. Grep rather than trust the line numbers.\n\nDECIDE PER SITE, do not sweep blindly. Some may genuinely mean \"was it WRITTEN with this keyword\" (a diagnostic that echoes the source, reflect's `kind` string). Those must stay `kind_of` and say so at the site. The rest are membership questions and should switch.\n\nACCEPTANCE: each site either switched or annotated with why it is a display question; cargo-test green; name which tests fail when the change is backed out (WI-956's experience: for most of these, NOTHING fails without a purpose-built fixture — say so rather than implying a test justifies it).\n\nSOURCE: WI-956 item 4."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
